&#x27; 42,78\&quot;&quot;]<br>angle sum printed: &quot;180° 0&#x27; 14,34\&quot;&quot;<br>sides printed: [&quot;log s = 5,0959243 (Anschluss an die Princ. Triang.), side opposite Saint Peters&quot;, &quot;log s = 4,8919727 (Anschluss an die Princ. Triang.), side opposite W42 Dünkirchen&quot;, &quot;log s = 4,8826525 (Anschluss an die Princ. Triang.), side opposite Fairlight&quot;]<br>page: &quot;Börsch &amp; Krüger 1896, p. 61, Französisches Kanalnetz Nr. 6&quot;]]></description><styleUrl>#t3</styleUrl><Polygon><tessellate>1</tessellate><outerBoundaryIs><LinearRing><coordinates>1.4187090,51.3653430,0 2.3764710,51.0356640,0 0.6190030,50.8773640,0 1.4187090,51.3653430,0</coordinates></LinearRing></outerBoundaryIs></Polygon></Placemark></Folder><Folder><name>France, arc of the parallel of 43 32 N, Pilier de Sette to Signal de Sainte Victoire (Cassini de Thury and Lacaille, 1739-1740) (8 stations, 6 triangles)</name><Placemark><name>Pilier de Sette (Mont de Sette, beside the Hermitage de S. Clair)</name><description><![CDATA[43 24 3 (table p. 290); also 43° 24&#x27; 6&quot; (p. 108)<br>21 14 17 (longitude counted from the meridian of the Isle de Fer, on which Paris = 19° 53&#x27; 10&quot;); difference of meridians in time 5&#x27; 24 1/2&quot; ori. (east of Paris). lon is CALC: (21 14 17 - 19 53 10) + Paris-Greenwich 9m 20.932s (Darwin 1908 p. 111)<br>cassini1744, pp. 108, 290]]></description><styleUrl>#st</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>3.6891610,43.4008330,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Tour de Salon (T. Septentr. du Ch. de Salon; east end of the Crau base)</name><description><![CDATA[43 38 20 (table p. 290, row &#x27;Salon&#x27;)<br>22 39 18 from the Isle de Fer meridian; 11&#x27; 4 1/2&quot; ori. in time from Paris (p. 290). lon is CALC as for Sette. The table row is &#x27;Salon&#x27;; that it is the same tower as the base end is inferred from its reference object Lebre<br>cassini1744, pp. 99, 290]]></description><styleUrl>#st</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>5.1061060,43.6388890,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Signal de Sainte Victoire</name><description><![CDATA[43° 31&#x27; 52 1/2&quot; (p. 108)<br>not printed as a longitude. Printed: arc sV = 78663,6 toises from the meridian of Sette (p. 104); fire-signal difference 1° 53&#x27; 19&quot; Sette to the Hermitage of Ste Victoire, which is 64 toises west of the signal (pp. 105-106). lon CALC = Sette lon + 78663,6 / 41618 toises per degree (p. 106)<br>cassini1744, pp. 104-106, 108]]></description><styleUrl>#st</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>5.5792950,43.5312500,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Signal des Houpies</name><description><![CDATA[not printed as a latitude. Printed colatitude PH = 46° 17&#x27; 8&quot; (p. 103), on Cassini&#x27;s working value PV = 46° 28&#x27; (Ste Victoire 43° 32&#x27;); lat = 90 - PH (CALC)<br>not printed. Printed arc kV = 24785,2 toises west of the meridian of Ste Victoire (p. 104); lon CALC = Ste Victoire lon - kV / 41618<br>cassini1744, pp. 103-104]]></description><styleUrl>#st</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>4.9837550,43.7144440,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Moulin de Calvisson</name><description><![CDATA[not printed as a latitude. Printed colatitude PC = 46° 13&#x27; 3&quot; (p. 104); lat = 90 - PC (CALC)<br>not printed. Printed arc ck = 33149,5 toises west of the meridian of Houpies (p. 104); lon CALC = Houpies lon - ck / 41618<br>cassini1744, p. 104]]></description><styleUrl>#st</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>4.1872360,43.7825000,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Colombier de Lebre</name><description><![CDATA[<br><br>cassini1744, pp. 102, 261-263 (no printed position; lat/lon CALC by plane resection from Ste Victoire with printed angles, printed side ratios and printed azimuth of Houpies to Ste Victoire 67 7 50 occ., using 57048 toises per degree of latitude (p. 103) and 41618 toises per degree of longitude (p. 106) scaled by cos latitude)]]></description><styleUrl>#st</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>5.0429870,43.4509130,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Signal de la Crau (west end of the Crau base, by the Lieutenance)</name><description><![CDATA[<br><br>cassini1744, pp. 99, 102, 262 (no printed position; lat/lon CALC by plane resection from Ste Victoire with printed angles, printed side ratios and printed azimuth of Houpies to Ste Victoire 67 7 50 occ., using 57048 toises per degree of latitude (p. 103) and 41618 toises per degree of longitude (p. 106) scaled by cos latitude)]]></description><styleUrl>#st</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>4.8726430,43.6424900,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Les Saintes Maries (church terrace; site of the powder fire signal)</name><description><![CDATA[<br><br>cassini1744, pp. 98, 102, 258, 261 (no printed position; lat/lon CALC by plane resection from Ste Victoire with printed angles, printed side ratios and printed azimuth of Houpies to Ste Victoire 67 7 50 occ., using 57048 toises per degree of latitude (p. 103) and 41618 toises per degree of longitude (p. 106) scaled by cos latitude)]]></description><styleUrl>#st</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>4.4308070,43.4578570,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Tour de Salon (T. Septentr. du Ch. de Salon; east end of the Crau base) - Signal de la Crau (west end of the Crau base, by the Lieutenance) - Colombier de Lebre</name><description><![CDATA[angles printed: {&quot;reduced_to_centre_and_horizon&quot;: {&quot;Tour de Salon&quot;: &quot;78 5 13 1/2&quot;, &quot;Signal de la Crau&quot;: &quot;57 4 43 1/2&quot;, &quot;Colombier de Lebre&quot;: &quot;44 49 47&quot;}, &quot;corrected_to_180&quot;: {&quot;Tour de Salon&quot;: &quot;78 5 20&quot;, &quot;Signal de la Crau&quot;: &quot;57 4 49&quot;, &quot;Colombier de Lebre&quot;: &quot;44 49 51&quot;}}<br>angle sum printed: &quot;179 59 44 (sum of the reduced angles, p. 102); corrected angles sum to 180 0 0&quot;<br>sides printed: {&quot;Signal de l